Goals
=====
Store Forwarding
----------------
    Allow loads to get values from the youngest older(**) store
    > where one or both loads/stores are dynamic. Dynamic load/stores 
      are those whose target addresses are not known at instruction 
      scheduling time e.g., pointers)
    > (**) this is also why Store Queues are age ordered)


Detect Intra Thread RAW violations
----------------------------------
    // *a->b = 0xabcd
        r0 = load P
    	store (r0 + 10, 0xabcd) << ------ 'X'

    // func(*c->b)
        r1 = load Q
	r1 = load (r1 + 10)     << ------ 'Y'
	call(r1)

    Its possible Load at 'Y' is issued before Store at 'X' is issued or the Store
    address known. Therefore even though the former load searches the Store Queue
    it won't find a match.

    There are roughly two simple solutions to this:
    [i]  Force stores to search Load Queue (assumes all non store buffer hitting
         loads are added to LQ) If found squash it and flush pipeline

    [ii] Instead of hurting the critical path, you check each LQ entry with SQ
         entries at the same address while committing instructions in ROB.

